    {
      "id": "claims-and-criticism",
      "name": "Claims and criticism",
      "group": "Claims",
      "layer": "terrain",
      "accuracy": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "verified",
      "scene": "terrain",
      "schematic": false,
      "material": "sand",
      "description": "This panel is the public argument about Lazar's account, not a feature on the ground. Schools he named have said they have no record of the degrees he claimed. A 1982 Los Alamos Monitor article and a Los Alamos phone-directory listing are the documents usually cited to show he was associated with the laboratory. They do not establish the job he described. Element 115, which he said powered the craft, was synthesized in 2003 and later named moscovium. Its known isotopes are short-lived. That synthesis does not confirm a stable isotope with the gravity effects he described. The disputes are part of the public record. His account of the craft and of S-4 remains testimony.",
